\title{Proving GCDRec correct}
\date{2026-09-02T13:42:38Z}
\tag{algorithms}
\tag{draft}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\p{We will begin by formally proving the correctness of [the recursive
Euclidean Algorithm](00K4). But before we can even do that, we have to
back up a bit: what does it even mean for an algorithm to be
"correct"?}

\transclude{00K6}  % specification vs implementation

\p{In this case, the \em{specification} we have in mind is the mathematical definition of #{gcd}; the implementation we have in mind is the #{\mathsf{GCDRec}} function.  We are starting with #{\mathsf{GCDRec}} because it's usually much easier to prove things about recursive algorithms than about iterative ones!}
